                },
                {
                  "id": "p-insurance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Insurance costs are a major factor when owning any truck body. Fortunately, insuring a used dry freight truck body is typically less expensive than insuring a new one. Since insurance premiums are based on your equipment’s current market value, a used truck body’s lower initial cost translates into lower monthly premiums and reduced long-term expenses.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-insurance-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Additionally, used truck bodies experience less depreciation than new ones, meaning their replacement costs are generally lower—another factor that contributes to decreased insurance rates. This makes owning a used truck body more cost-effective and sustainable over the long run.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
